# A committed TEMPLATE of .github/c2-serving-job.env for the tp4/draft-vocab four-card DEVELOPMENT window (scripts/ci/c2_serving_job.py parses it): copy it over
# .github/c2-serving-job.env on a throwaway commit of tp4/draft-vocab and push a tag experiment/c2-serving-vN. Nothing here names a rig, a card, a host or a registry: the cards
# are resolved at run time. The jobs are templates only: no tag is pushed from this branch by its author. ORDER.txt has the order, the stop rules, the minutes and the read rules.
# ONE IMAGE FOR THE WHOLE WINDOW: C2_IMAGE_TAG=tp4-dvocab-1 is a PLACEHOLDER for the tag B0 builds from the pushed branch head (sed -i 's/tp4-dvocab-1/<tag>/' *.env). A commit of a file the image
# carries needs a new B0 build and a new tag in every template. The cards are under development: this window never stops, starts or hands back the node agent.
# D-V2: the coding draft-vocabulary tau arm dvocab: the served drafter with QWEN_FAST_DRAFT_VOCAB=coding-40960 (docs/tp4-draft-vocab.md): the drafter proposes from 40,960 of the 248,320 rows, a sliced copy
# of the target head built at the attach; the target verifies every row of the whole vocabulary, so the text is the control's and ONLY THE ACCEPTED LENGTH MOVES (a token outside the list can never be
# proposed). It runs on the control image tp4-dvocab-1 like dedf-bf16 and lookup: no new image, no A3. Before pushing, REPLACE @CONTROL_RUN@ with the run id of D-V1 (digits; the job reader refuses this
# template without it). The attach logs '[PINDIAG] draft vocab admitted' and '... head built' (launched_problems holds the arm to both before anything is sent: a flag that never crossed into the container
# would measure the control under this arm's name) and the first draft pass logs '... engaged' (the CANARY after the first turns holds it). The tau profile is c2-packed-tp4 (single-user draft passes, 16-row
# blocks): the pooled ratio is the shortlist's tau cost on real coding text with thinking ON; the timing pack (TV1-TV4) is where the round time it buys is judged. Judged PAIRED per turn id by
# drafter_pair_report.py against the control arm (the GO rule is in its docstring and docs/drafter-arms.md): NONINFERIORITY, not gain, for this arm (a shortlist can only remove proposals): the pooled
# ratio's 95% lower bound above 0.97 (the tau cost a ~3.5% eight-live round saving pays for), no regression in the 80k+ bucket or at p10, identical text, both runs launched clean and asked the same
# questions, equal image tags. A GO here says the tau cost is small; whether the round time it buys outweighs it is the timing pack's (TV1-TV4, draft_vocab_report.py, docs/tp4-draft-vocab.md section 5).
# Duration (estimate): 85 min (the deadline of 80 min is counted from the container start, the load included). Kill rule: the launched-argv check or the canary finding no draft-vocabulary line, a
# stall or a tripped breaker ends the arm.
C2_CARDS=quad
C2_ACTIONS=reset taulab
C2_IMAGE_TAG=tp4-dvocab-1
C2_TAULAB_PROFILE=c2-packed-tp4
C2_TAULAB_DRAFTER_ARM=dvocab
C2_TAULAB_ARMS=A1 A2
C2_TAULAB_DEADLINE=80
C2_TAULAB_IN_FLIGHT=8
C2_TAULAB_PAIR_CONTROL=@CONTROL_RUN@
